            </profile>
            <profile id="7688-798a-ce7a-c683" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Equipment as for the Army General. Army General. Must always deploy first. The enemy player rolls a D6 at the start of the game: the result is the number of times he may require the Roman player to re-roll a Leadership test (no single test more than once). In compensation the Roman player receives one free Military Tribune or Prefect of the Allies (basic 69 pts, no options). Use only via the Alternative Generals roll. (Hannibal p.56)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="c33c-ac76-2c35-49a7" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
