            <profile id="d2f5-81ec-0866-8ca8" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Equipment as for the Army General; if mounted may ride a Warhorse instead (M8 WS3 BS0 S3 I3 A1). Army General, Drilled, Stubborn. Always deploys second. The Roman player rolls a D6 at the start of the game: the result is the number of times he may re-roll a Leadership test (no single test more than once). Use only via the Alternative Generals roll. (Hannibal p.56)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="661c-decc-b4b7-c39a" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">None</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
