  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="4310-1cc8-abd3-5361" name="Republican Roman (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>REPUBLICAN ROMAN ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.51-62)
Characters up to 25% of points; at least one character must be the Army General. Common and Uncommon limits and membership depend on the chosen campaign (force entry). "R:" = restricted: a unit of the listed type must be taken first (not enforced).
Unit upgrades: minimum 5 models per unit, no maximum. One model may be upgraded to Leader, Standard Bearer and Musician (+5 each), but Hastati, Principes and Triarii get them free.
Reorganisation (use Velites instead of Leves; two units of Principes per unit of Triarii; field one Triarii unit per two Hastati and two Principes).
Latin allies: use the Roman profiles (or Italian Spearmen for the early Republic). Allies (p.61, not enforced): Gallic Tribes (Gallic list; one northern Italian tribe, no other allies), Spanish (with Numidians only), Numidian (with Spanish only), Hellenistic Greek (Armies of Antiquity; with Pergamenes only, no Spartans), Pergamene (Alexander and his Successors list). Allies do not gain the Roman leadership benefits.
Optional rules (p.62): Fortified Camp, Penal and Slave Legions (use Leves and Accensi entries with mixed weapons; Hate any enemy; heavy infantry cause fear; take Leadership tests to pursue/collect heads), Unbridled Charge.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Republican Roman - First Punic War]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 75%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 10%
  Common: Leves; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry; Italian Spearmen.
  Uncommon: Rorarii; Accensi.
[Republican Roman - Second Punic War in Spain]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 75%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 10%
  Common: Leves OR Velites; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry; Italian Spearmen.
  Uncommon: Spanish Infantry; Spanish Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry).
[Republican Roman - Second Punic War in Italy]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 75%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 10%
  Common: Leves OR Velites; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry; Italian Spearmen.
  Uncommon: Cretan Archers; Syracusan Skirmishers; Tarentine Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry).
[Republican Roman - Second and Third Punic Wars in Africa]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 75%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 5%
  Common: Velites; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry.
  Uncommon: Syracusan Skirmishers.
[Republican Roman - Campaigns in the West]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 65%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 20%
  Common: Velites; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry.
  Uncommon: Tarentine Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry); Numidian Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry); Spanish Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry); Gallic Infantry; Gallic Cavalry (R: Gallic Infantry).
[Republican Roman - Campaigns in the East]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Common Troops: at least 65%
  Uncommon Troops: up to 20%
  Common: Velites; Hastati; Principes; Triarii; Roman and Italian Cavalry; Thureophoroi and Peltasts.
  Uncommon: Cretan Archers; Tarentine Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry); Numidian Cavalry (R: Roman and Italian Cavalry); Spanish Infantry; Spanish Cavalry (R: Spanish Infantry); Gallic Infantry; Gallic Cavalry (R: Gallic Infantry); Illyrian Infantry; Illyrian Cavalry (R: Illyrian Infantry); Ligurian Infantry; 0-1 Elephant.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
